  "notes": "Three lithium-ion chemistries (LFP, NMC, NCA); file names give cell, C-rate and temperature. Surface temperature is measured with T-type thermocouples. The delivered LFP discharge filenames include 20C tests; the earlier 5C scalar was a modal per-entity attribute, not the maximum across all test parts. The 20C maximum applies to LFP tests, not every cell chemistry."
=======
  "notes": "Three lithium-ion chemistries (LFP, NMC, NCA); file names give cell, C-rate and temperature. Surface temperature is measured with T-type thermocouples. The delivered LFP discharge filenames include 20C tests; the earlier 5C scalar was a modal per-entity attribute, not the maximum across all test parts. The 20C maximum applies to LFP tests, not every cell chemistry. Charging profile: the charge is the same CC-CV in every file; the C-rate differs between files and cells through the discharge current. The data article (Catenaro and Onori, Data in Brief 35 (2021) 106894; full text read) confirms and extends the record: six samples (k1-k6) of each of three cells, Panasonic NCR-18650B NCA (3350 mAh), LG Chem INR21700-M50 NMC (4850 mAh) and A123 Systems ANR26650m1-B LFP (2500 mAh), all with graphite anodes, tested at 5, 25 and 35 C (IncuMax IC-500R chamber, Arbin LBT21024, 1 s sampling, T-type thermocouple on the cell centre measuring the skin temperature, unfiltered data). Charging is CC-CV at the manufacturer-specified current (the value is not given), then CV to a cut-off current (NCA, NMC) or for 1 h (LFP); discharge rates are C/20, 1C, 2C, 3C, 5C for NCA and NMC and also 10C, 15C and 20C for LFP, to 2.5 V (NCA, NMC) or 2 V (LFP), with a stop at 75 C. The three cells have three different formats: 18650, 21700 and 26650. The dataset-level format code 18650 and the 18 x 65 mm dimensions inferred from it describe only the NCA cell; they come from the registry and are listed in the discrepancy matrix. The related analysis paper is Catenaro, Rizzo and Onori, Applied Energy 2021, 10.1016/j.apenergy.2021.116473. The dataset-level format code and the 18 x 65 mm dimensions are left null on purpose: the three chemistries come in three formats. Rate combinations: the charge is CC-CV at the manufacturer-specified current, which the data article does not state, so the charge C-rate is null for every discharge rate listed."
